            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Domestic Policy and the \"Jamahiriya\" System</strong><br>\nGaddafi introduced the \"Jamahiriya,\" or \"state of the masses,\" in Libya, which he claimed was a form of direct democracy, though in practice it was considered authoritarian, with power concentrated in his hands.</p>\n\n<p><strong>c1</strong><br>\nEarly Life and Education</p>\n\n<p><strong>Kurt Waldheim was born in 1918 in Sankt Andrä-Wördern, Austria. He studied law at the University of Vienna, where he received a doctorate in 1944. His early career was marked by his service in the Austrian army during World War II, which later became a subject of international controversy regarding his role during the war.</strong><br>\nUnited Nations Secretary-General</p>\n"
              },
